# Dev server lifecycle (agents)

`langflower start` and `npm run dev` are **long-running** processes. Do not leave
them running when you finish a task.

## Default

- **Do not** start the dev server in the **background** unless the user explicitly
  asks to keep it running for manual testing.
- Prefer **one-shot verification** that exits on its own:
  - `node build/tools/agent-run.mjs verify` — build + unit + integration (~1 min);
    this is the close-out gate
  - `node build/tools/agent-run.mjs verify --quick` — build + unit only
    (intermediate; not enough to mark a feature done)
  - `node build/test.mjs --integration` — after a local `build-all`, when you
    changed execution / WS / bootstrap / agent flows only
  - Short `curl` / WebSocket probe, then exit

## If you must start the server

1. Run in the **foreground** with a bounded check, or in background only when the
   user requested it.
2. **Stop the server before ending your turn** — do not assume the user will kill it.
3. On Windows (Git Bash): find PID on port 4010 and terminate:

```bash
netstat -ano | grep ':4010' | grep LISTENING
taskkill //F //PID <pid>
```

4. If port 4010 is busy at startup, stop the existing process first — do not start
   a second server.

## When the user wants the server running

Only then may you leave it up — say clearly that it is still running and on which
port.
